Patch 2017: shadow-map depth-compare descriptors in the D3D12 fragment path (for the RSX depth texture formats 0x90-0x93).

The draw's unit state goes through rsx_fp_shadow_desc_from_texture into rsx_fp_decompile_buffered_shadow_ex; the packed descriptors
are part of the pipeline key. RSX_SHADOW_CMP=0 turns it off. [SHUNIT]/[SHADOW] log lines name the sampled units >= 4.

Re-fitted for v0.19.0: Carries #618's unnormalized inputs next to the shadow bytes. A shadow-compare unit is left out of #618's coordinate scaling: the shadow helper divides an unnormalized coordinate by the size itself.

